      4     0.2500           4.6812e-11    0.2183  +0.1620 |   5.6560e-11    0.1981  +0.1364
  [PASS] V2 [THE TEST: which integer the real rotation curves prefer, with nothing fitted] the root-mean-square residual of the radial acceleration relation is computed for each integer on both density conventions, and the preferred integer identified
         measured: dark-energy convention: best n = 2 at 0.1502 dex; critical-density convention: best n = 2 at 0.1438 dex
         reading : the data pick n = 2 on both conventions, with no fitted quantity anywhere -- not the acceleration scale, not a shape parameter. n = 2 is what kappa = 1/2 requires

